 like an ordinary girl who loves fun things and her boyfriend Shuri, she's actually a super-genius who gets the top score on every test. She becomes student council president and tries to make school life more fun in various ways.\n<br><br>\n(Source: Anime News Network)", "startDate": {"year": 2014, "month": 8}, "endDate": {"year": 2015, "month": 12}, "season": "SUMMER", "seasonYear": 2014, "episodes": 6, "duration": 13, "countryOfOrigin": "JP", "source": "MANGA", "hashtag": null, "genres": ["Comedy", "Romance"], "tags": [{"name": "School", "rank": 79, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Shoujo", "rank": 79, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Idol", "rank": 20, "isAdult": false}]}, {"id": 21624, "title": {"romaji": "Steins;Gate: Kyoukaimenjou no Missing Link - Divide By Zero", "english": "Steins;Gate 0: 23β -Divide by Zero-"}, "format": "OVA", "description": "Alternate 23rd episode of Steins;Gate, which leads into the story of Steins;Gate 0. Included with the Steins;Gate Complete Blu-ray Box.<br>\n<br>\nThe main difference between this episode and the original episode 23 is that Okabe does not receive the Movie Mail from his future self, due to Mayuri begging Suzuha to stop relying on Okabe to prevent World War Three. By not opening the Movie Mail Okabe does not find out about Operation Skuld and is unsuccessful in averting both Kurisu's death and World War Three, thereby leading into the story of Steins;Gate 0<br>", "startDate": {"year": 2015, "month": 12}, "endDate": {"year": 2015, "month": 12}, "season": "FALL", "seasonYear": 2015, "episodes": 1, "duration": 24, "countryOfOrigin": "JP", "source": "VISUAL_NOVEL", "hashtag": null, "genres": ["Drama", "Psychological", "Sci-Fi", "Thriller"], "tags": [{"name": "Tragedy", "rank": 90, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Alternate Universe", "rank": 90, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Time Manipulation", "rank": 89, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "War", "rank": 70, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Urban", "rank": 70, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Kuud